+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"observation","id":"obs_01M2GH5AQRSY0RP6PSYGAV58MW","companyId":"example-co","controlIds":["rbi-outsourcing-risk-directions-2025:97(vii)"],"title":"Containers deployed to AWS EKS (third-party cloud, NBFC middle-layer outsourcing) are unsigned and lack a governed SBOM","description":"applications/mcp-gateway/env/prod.json and qa.json place the mcp-gateway image on AWS EKS in ap-south-1 (eks-prod-mumbai / eks-nonprod-mumbai), a third-party cloud arrangement under example-co's NBFC middle-layer registration. The image built by docker-publish.yml has no cosign signature, no attested SBOM and no workspace image governance record, so the outsourcing-directions container-governance expectation is not met.","methods":["probe-cicd-env"],"subjects":[{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"}],"collectedAt":"2026-09-14T13:48:42Z","expiresAt":"2026-10-14T13:48:42Z","result":"not-satisfied","toolOutput":{"format":"sarif","path":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/1a5b055e-58b2-4969-9611-d47c345c064a/probe-cicd-env.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","sha256":"dc357366ff0f5fbd47e3a1b9e407d5d877f6c5dc16552f0f4c709686ba3c151d"},"evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/env/prod.json","description":"AWS EKS ap-south-1 hosting"},{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/1a5b055e-58b2-4969-9611-d47c345c064a/probe-cicd-env.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","description":"CICD-SIGN-01, CICD-SBOM-02 results","sha256":"dc357366ff0f5fbd47e3a1b9e407d5d877f6c5dc16552f0f4c709686ba3c151d"}],"tags":["cicd","supply-chain","static-probe"],"recordedAt":"2026-09-14T14:46:47Z","provenance":{"harness":"claude-code","generatedAt":"2026-09-14T13:48:42Z","sessionId":"1a5b055e-58b2-4969-9611-d47c345c064a","runId":"run_01M2FGNVVQ15ZKXZWGW74YWAAQ","workflow":"probe-cicd-env","agent":"soc-ledger-keeper"}}
+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GH5AS0MM2F8MSFTDP36VV9","companyId":"example-co","title":"Both Dockerfiles pin node:24-alpine with no content digest","description":"Dockerfile:1 and deploy/aws/Dockerfile:2 both read `FROM node:24-alpine` with no `@sha256:...` digest, so the runtime base of the image behind the order-routing critical function (applications/mcp-gateway/env/prod.json, eks-prod-mumbai) floats to whatever node:24-alpine currently resolves to at build time. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.MA.S3-mapped applicable control PR.IP.S1 (high). SLA topic: patch-sla.\n\nRefutation: evidence lens not refuted (Evidence holds: Dockerfile:1 and deploy/aws/Dockerfile:2 both read `FROM node:24-alpine` with no digest, and no @sha256 pin, base-image build arg or override appears anywhere else in the checkout. The SARIF export has a CICD-PIN-02 fail result at Dockerfile lines 1-1 with maxwell/v1 fingerprint 6c113f0c...5974, the same regulatory refs, invocation executionSuccessful true, revisionId equal to pinnedCommit and the same session and run. details.json links critical function order-routing to mcp-gateway, and prod.json (tier prod, exposure partner, cluster eks-prod-mumbai) points iac at this repo's deploy/ path. Severity high stands, but not for the reason the record gives: catalog PR.DS.S6 applies only to reCategories mii and qualified-re, while example-co is registered as mid-size-re. So the \"catalog defaultSeverity\" basis is doubtful under regulatory-mapping, and high still follows from the SARIF level error under maxwell-conventions section 4 step 3. Two further notes: deploy/aws/README.md describes that Dockerfile as a Bedrock AgentCore image pushed to ECR in us-east-1, so tying it to eks-prod-mumbai is an inference, not something the files state. And the remediation text is wrong in one place: .github/dependabot.yml already has a docker entry, but only for directory \"/\", so deploy/aws/Dockerfile is not covered. (Unverifiable: the export sha256 dc357366... could not be recomputed and no other recorded digest exists to compare it with.)); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (The cited clause sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S6 does not bind example-co: its catalog applicability is reCategories [mii, qualified-re] and its prose says 'Exempt for Mid-size, Small-size and Self-certification REs', while both of example-co's SEBI registrations are mid-size-re; no sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S6 control record exists in soc/main.jsonl either, so controlIds would dangle. The mapping is repairable with sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S1 (mandatory for all REs, no reCategory limit; its prose requires 'deploying only hardened and vetted hardware and software', which an unpinned floating node:24-alpine base breaks). A control record for it exists in the ledger and its defaultSeverity is high, so severity=high stays correct. SEBI stays first, and nist-ssdf-800-218 (global, empty applicability) stays as a secondary ref next to PR.IP.S1's catalog mapping nist-csf-2.0 PR.PS-01. The description text naming 'PR.DS.S6 (high)' should be updated to match. Note PR.IP.S1's probeWorkflows list does not include probe-cicd-env, but no category-unrestricted CSCRF control that does list it (PR.IP.S4 scanning, PR.MA.S3 patching) covers base-image pinning as directly.).","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S1"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.IP.S1"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-csf-2.0","controlId":"PR.PS-01"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-ssdf-800-218","controlId":"PW.4.4"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"Dockerfile","startLine":1,"endLine":1},"fingerprint":"6c113f0c1e613589795d4adeac167a6eb56c9e169f67c99337b4455f30ff5974","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"CICD-PIN-02","tool":"maxwell-cicd-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"open","slaDu