+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GH5B0C1BP3QP8HHA0MJNVY","companyId":"example-co","title":"Published image is never signed or attested with cosign","description":"docker-publish.yml:78-89 pushes the image to Docker Hub with buildx `provenance: mode=max` and `sbom: true`, but no `cosign sign` (keyless OIDC or KMS key) and no `cosign attest` step exists anywhere in the 20 workflows, so an admission controller (e.g. Kyverno verifyImages) or a manual puller has no signature to check against the digest. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.IP.S2 (medium), cited because the nearer control sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.DS.S6 is exempt for mid-size REs. SLA topic: patch-sla.\n\nRefutation: evidence lens not refuted (docker-publish.yml lines 78-89 push with provenance mode=max and sbom true and no signing step anywhere in the checkout; SARIF result CICD-SIGN-01 matches at the same fingerprint.); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S6 does not bind example-co -- reCategories mii/qualified-re only, mid-size-re is exempt, and no control record exists for it. The nearest applicable SEBI clause is PR.IP.S2 (SDLC with security stages, mandatory, no reCategory restriction, control record present, defaultSeverity medium), so severity becomes medium. rbi-outsourcing-risk-directions-2025:97(vii) (cloud/container governance, binds nbfc-middle-layer, control record present) is a valid secondary ref after the SEBI ref; nist-ssdf-800-218 PS.2.1 is a valid global mapping.)","severity":"medium","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S2","rbi-outsourcing-risk-directions-2025:97(vii)"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.IP.S2"},{"regulator":"RBI","instrument":"rbi-outsourcing-risk-directions-2025","controlId":"97(vii)"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-ssdf-800-218","controlId":"PS.2.1"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-ser