+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GH5B1JFJYTA2MGWES48JP5","companyId":"example-co","title":"SBOM generated by CI is never captured into the workspace image inventory for mcp-gateway","description":"docker-publish.yml:87 sets `sbom: true` on the buildx build-push step, which would attach a CycloneDX/SPDX attestation to the pushed image, but no applications/mcp-gateway/images/ directory or record exists in the workspace at all -- Scout confirmed no imageId or sbomPath is linked to this repo. Per the present-but-empty-SBOM rule an SBOM step whose output is never attached, uploaded or attested to the workspace is treated as a missing SBOM. mcp-gateway's container backs the order-routing critical function (company-profile/example-co/details.json criticalFunctions[0]) and runs in prod with pii/financial data. No image record exists so this targets the repo rather than an imageId. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 GV.SC.S5 (high). SLA topic: sbom.\n\nRefutation: evidence lens not refuted (docker-publish.yml line 87 sets sbom: true; no export, upload or attest step exists anywhere in the checkout; no image records exist under applications/mcp-gateway; SARIF export has a matching CICD-SBOM-02 fail result; severity high matches the GV.SC.S5 catalog defaultSeverity, whose control record exists in the ledger.); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (sebi-cscrf-2024:GV.SC.S5 is in scope for example-co, exists in the catalog, covers a missing SBOM for a critical system and is cited first; its defaultSeverity is high; rbi-outsourcing-risk-directions-2025:97(vii) is a valid secondary cloud/container-governance ref with a ledger control record; nist-ssdf-800-218 PS.3.2 is a catalog mapping of GV.SC.S5.)","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:GV.SC.S5"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"GV.SC.S5"},{"regulator":"RBI","instrument":"rbi-outsourcing-risk-directions-2025","controlId":"97(vii)"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-ssdf-800-218","controlId":"PS.3.2"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":".github/workflows/docker-publish.yml","startLine":78,"endLine":89},"fingerprint":"5d0f217b909420d9f1716c30dcdef0adbf9f825f9f82cc195221bd0288c65a53","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"CICD-SBOM-02","tool":"maxwell-cicd-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"open","slaDueAt":"2026-10-14T13:48:42Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","days":30},"relatedObservationIds":["obs_01M2GH5AEWAEG67SKAJ51YWA44"],"firstSeenAt":"2026-09-14T13:48:42Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-14T13:48:42Z","evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/.github/workflows/docker-publish.yml","description":"sbom: true step, unevidenced"},{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/1a5b055e-58b2-4969-9611-d47c345c064a/probe-cicd-env.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","description":"CICD-SBOM-02 result","sha256":"dc357366ff0f5fbd47e3a1b9e407d5d877f6c5dc16552f0f4c709686ba3c151d"}],"tags":["cicd","supply-chain","static-probe","sbom-missing"],"recordedAt":"2026-09-14T14:46:47Z","provenance":{"harness":"claude-code","generatedAt":"2026-09-14T13:48:42Z","sessionId":"1a5b055e-58b2-4969-9611-d47c345c064a","runId":"run_01M2FGNVVQ15ZKXZWGW74YWAAQ","workflow":"probe-cicd-env","agent":"soc-ledger-keeper"}}
+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GH5B2SNX0PD3EKVNVTPAG7","companyId":"example-co","title":"Docker Hub publish uses a static shared credential instead of the OIDC federation already used elsewhere in the repo","description":"docker-publish.yml:72-76 authenticates to Docker Hub with `secrets.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME`/`secrets.DOCKERHUB_PASSWORD`, a long-lived shared credential. mcp-publish.yml:24-25 in the same repository federates to the MCP registry via `mcp-publisher login github-oidc` and needs no stored secret, demonstrating the OIDC pattern is available and used elsewhere but not applied to the higher-traffic Docker Hub publish. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S1 (high).\n\nRefutation: evidence lens not refuted (docker-publish.yml:72-76 logs in with static secrets; mcp-publish.yml:24-25 in the same repo uses OIDC federation with no stored secret; SARIF export has a matching CICD-SEC-01 fail result; high severity is the defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S1.); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (sebi-cscrf-2024 applies, PR.AA.S1 exists in the catalog and ledger and its prose covers issuing, managing and auditing credentials for CI processes; the dpdp-rules-2025 secondary ref proposed elsewhere is dropped because Rules 3 and 5-16 are not yet in force and the credential is not tied to personal-data processing; nist-800-53-r5 IA-5 accurately names authenticator management and matches the SARIF result.)","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S1"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.AA.S1"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-800-53-r5","controlId":"IA-5"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":".github/workflows/docker-publish.yml","startLine":72,"endLine":76},"fingerprint":"b06d8ecbc490be1ebb8a362b04f4ce828b0f327ec523d0fcdc20bdaf43060160","source":{"kind":"sarif",